<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75813" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλαί</span></b> , 
			Att.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλαί</span></b> , αἱ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>barley-corns,
				barley-groats</i>, which were sprinkled on the head of the
			victim before the sacrifice (cf. Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1164
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				3.441
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				1.132
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				1167
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pax</u>
				948
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				960
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Char.</u>
				10.13
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλ-</span>, 
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλ-</span>
			), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1024.18
			</span></i> (Myconos, <span class="entity">iii/ii B. C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλαὶ κριθῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					1.160
				</span></i>
			. (The variation <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐλαί</span>:
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλαί</span> points to orig. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀλϝαί</span>, cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλβάχνιον</span>: the <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
			</span></i> form 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀλοαί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(2).514.15
				</span></i>
			 (Lycosura, <span class="entity">ii B. C.</span>) prob. comes from a bye-form
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀλοϝαί</span>. Perh. cogn.
			with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀλέω</span> (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλυμος</span> III, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄλυρα</span>.)</div>
